$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Trifluoromethyl Silyl Ethers (R)-10-12: To a solution of ketoamide 4-6 (1
equiv) and trifluoromethyl(trimethyl)silane (1.2 equiv) in DMF was added,
at rt under Ar, potassium carbonate (0.05-0.15 equiv). After the complete
conversion of starting ketoamide (reaction monitored by GC), the reaction
was quenched with a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted
thrice with Et2O. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by chromatography (PE/Et2O) and recrystallised (for solid
compounds).
(–)-(4R,5R)-2,2-Dimethyl-5-((R)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenyl-1-trimethylsilanyloxy-ethyl)-[1,3]dioxolane-4-carboxylic
acid methoxy-methyl-amide (R)-10.
(-)-(4R,5R)-2,2-Dimethyl-5-((R)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenyl-1-trimethylsilanyloxy-ethyl)-[1,3]dioxolane-4-carboxylic
acid dimethylamide (R)-11, According to the general procedure, a mixture
of ketoamide 5 (197 mg, 0.71 mmol), CF3TMS (0. 13mL, 0.88 mmol, 1.2
equiv) and K2CO3 (11.1 mg, 0.08 mmol, 0.11 equiv) in DMF (3 mL) was
stirred for 2h30. Purification of the residue (mixture of two
diastereomers 93:7) by chromatography (PE/EtOAc 90:10) afforded the major
diastereomer (R)-11 (231 mg, 78 %) as a colourless oil. tR = 11.5
min.[α]D20 -20.4 (c 1.04, CHCl3);19F NMR (235.3 MHz) δ -75.5 (s, 3F,
CF3); 1H NMR (250 MHz) δ 0.17 (s, 9H), 1.33 (s, 3H), 1.43 (s, 3H), 2.97
(s, 3H), 3.03 (s, 3H), 4.55 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (d, J = 6.5 Hz,
1H), 7.35-7.38 (m, 3H), 7.66 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (62.9 MHz)δ 1.8, 25.8,
26.1, 35.8, 36.9, 73.0, 78.5, 80.1 (q, J = 27.5 Hz), 111.3, 124.7 (q, J
=287.5 Hz, CF3), 127.7, 128.1, 128.8, 135.5, 168.8. HRMS (ESI+): m/z
calcd for C19H28F3NO4SiNa [M+Na]+442.1637, found 442.1639.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 93:7 crude diastereomeric ratio, optimization study,
optimized on initiator, solvent and reaction temp.
