$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Addition of TMSCF3
to Aldehyde/ Ketone under Nucleophilic Catalysis in DMF. Aldehyde/ketone
(1 mmol) and TMSCF3 (neat) in dry DMF (3 mL) were placed in a 25 mL
round-bottom flask (or a 30 mL vial). To this solution was added
nucleophilic catalyst, and the mixture was stirred vigorously at room
temperature. Completion of the reaction was monitored by TLC and GCMS.
The reaction mixture was then poured in brine solution (15 mL) and
extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 30 mL). Combined organic layers were
finally washed with brine solution, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and then
solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The crude product was further
purified by chromatography (using 9:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate solvent
system) to afford pure TMS-protected alcohols.
Trimethyl-(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenyl-ethoxy)-silane (5a)
Trimethyl-[2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(4-nitro-phenyl)-ethoxy]-silane (5c)
Yellowish liquid, 1H NMR δ 0.17 (s, 9H), 5.08 (q, J = 6.30 Hz, 1H), 7.69
(d, J = 8.40 Hz, 2H), 8.12 (d, J = 8.98 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR δ -0.43, 72.4
(q, 2 J(C, F) = 32.20 Hz), 123.5, 124.0, 1 J(C, F) = 282.94 Hz), 128.5
142.3, 148.4 19F NMR δ -78.5 (d, 3 J(F, H) = 7.63 Hz); MS (EI), m/z 277.8
(M.+-CH3), 223.7 (M.+-CH3CF3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM trimethylamine N-oxide and potassium carbonate as alternate catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile Synthesis of TMS-Protected Trifluoromethylated Alcohols Using
Trifluoromethyltrimethylsilane (TMSCF3) and Various Nucleophilic
Catalysts in DMF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Prakash, G. K. Surya; Panja, Chiradeep; Vaghoo, Habiba; Surampudi,
Vijayalakshmi; Kultyshev, Roman; Mandal, Mihirbaran; Rasul, Golam;
Mathew, Thomas; Olah, George A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(18), 6806-6813

