$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To ketone (0.83 g, 5.0 rnmol) in a dry flask under Ng were added DMF
(anhydrous, 5 mL)and TMSCF3 (2.1 g, 15 -01). AAer the mixture was cooled
to -25 °C, carbene (0.5mmol) was added. The mixture was warmed to room
temperature and stirred at that temperature for 1 h. A 2 N HCl solution
(6 mL) was added and the solution was stirred atroom temperature until
all TMS protected intermediate converted to product. Water (30mL) was
added and the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (2 x 20 mL).
Thecombined organic layers were washed with saturated NaHC03 aqueous
solution (15 mL),brine (15 mL), and dried over MgS04. Solvents were
removed under vacuum to give thecrude residue, which was purified by
silica flash chromatography (10% to 30% ethylacetate in hexanes) to give
yield 0.88 g, 75%. 1 H NMR (CDC13, 500 MHz) δ8.24 (d, J = 8.75 Hz, 2H),
7.79 (d, J = 8.55 Hz, 2H), 2.54(brs, lH), 1.83 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCI,,
125 MHz) δ 151.2, 144.5, 126.8, 124.4 (q, JC-F = 284 Hz), 122.7, 23.4.
HRMS was run on the TMS protected product (APCI negative with
chloroacetonitrile): calc'd for C9H8N03F3Cl (loss of TMS, and chloride
adduct), calc'd m/z 270.0144, obs'd m/z 270.0162.
