$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Fe-Catalyzed
Trifluoromethylation of Aldehydes/Ketones. A 5 mM stock solution of
TBA[Fe] (10.3 mg, 0.025 mmol) and DMAP (3.05 mg, 0.025 mmol) in anhydrous
THF (5 mL) was prepared in a flame-dried Schlenk tube. Anhydrous THF (0.5
mL) and the stock solution (1.5 mL, 0.0075 mmol, 0.75 mol % TBAFe and
DMAP) were added to a flame-dried Schlenk tube. The appropriate aldehyde
(1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) and TMS-CF3 (296 μL, 2.00 mmol, 2 equiv) were added
under an atmosphere of N2, and the mixture was stirred for 14 h at 30°C.
The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel as indicated below to afford the
trifluoromethylated silyl ethers 4-24.
Trimethyl(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)ethoxy)silane (4).82 The
title compound was purified by chromatography on silica gel with PE/EtOAc
50/1 (v/v) as eluent,
2-(2,2,2-Trifluoro-1-((trimethylsilyl)oxy)ethyl)pyridine (14).85 The
title compound was purified by chromatography on silica gel with
npentane/Et2O 30/1 (v/v) to 10/1 (v/v) as eluent, 14 as a colorless oil
(183 mg, 74% yield). Rf = 0.25 (n-pentane/Et2O 10/1 (v/ v)); 1H NMR (250
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 8.56 (dq, J = 1.0 Hz, J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (td, J =
1.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (ddd, J = 1.5, 5.0, 7.5
Hz, 1H), 5.08 (q, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 0.11 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (63 MHz, CDCl3)
δ (ppm) 155.64 (C), 148.8 (CH), 136.8 (CH), 124.0 (q, J = 283.5 Hz, C),
123.8 (CH), 122.3 (CH), 74.7 (q, J = 31.5 Hz, CH), -0.4 (CH3); 19F NMR
(235 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) -77.7 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3F); IR (ATR) 3061, 3020,
2961, 1592, 1576, 1473, 1438, 1368 cm-1 ; HRMS (ESI): calcd for
[(C10H15F3NOSi)+ ] 250.0870, found 250.0865.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fe-Catalyzed Nucleophilic Activation of C-Si versus Allylic C-O Bonds:
Catalytic Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl Groups versus Tandem
Trifluormethylation-Allylation of Olefins
