$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for Nucleophilic Trifluoromethylation of aldimines with
TMSCF3. Under nitrogen atmosphere, into a 25 ml round-bottomed flask
containing benzilideneaniline 1a (181 mg, 1.0 mmol) and
tetrabutylammonium triphenyldifluorosilicate (TBAT) (81 mg, 0.15 mmol) in
THF (5 ml) at room temperature, was added dropwise TMSCF3 (213 mg, 1.5
mmol). via a syringe. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1 hour, and then quenched by adding 1N HCl aqueous
solution (0.2 ml). The quenched solution was washed with aqueous
saturated NaHCO3 solution followed by water and saturated aqueous NaCl
solution. The combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The residue was further
purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane : ethyl acetate = 9
: 1) to give N-(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenylethyl)aniline 3a (188 mg, 75%
yield) as a pale yellow oil. 1H NMR δ 4.32 (br. d, J= 7.3Hz, 1H), 4.91
(qd, J= 7.6, 7.3Hz, 1H), 6.62 (d, J= 7.9Hz, 2H), 6.76 (t, J= 7.5Hz, 1H),
7.14 (dd, J= 8.4, 7.5Hz, 2H), 7.32-7.45 (m, 5H); 19F NMR δ -74.5 (d, J=
7.6Hz, 3F); 13C NMR δ 60.5 (q, J= 29.8Hz), 113.9, 119.2, 125.1 (q, J=
282Hz), 127.9, 128.7, 128.9, 129.1, 129.4, 129.7; GCMS m/z 250 (M+-H),
181 (M+-CF3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Tri- and Difluoromethylated Amines from Aldimines Using
