$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Nucleophilic
Trifluoromethylation of aldimines with TMSCF3. Under nitrogen atmosphere,
into a 25 ml round-bottomed flask containing benzilideneaniline 1a (181
mg, 1.0 mmol) and tetrabutylammonium triphenyldifluorosilicate (TBAT) (81
mg, 0.15 mmol) in THF (5 ml) at room temperature, was added dropwise
TMSCF3 (213 mg, 1.5 mmol). via a syringe. The reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 1 hour, and then quenched by adding 1N
HCl aqueous solution (0.2 ml). The quenched solution was washed with
aqueous saturated NaHCO3 solution followed by water and saturated aqueous
NaCl solution. The combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4, filtered,
and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The residue was
further purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane : ethyl
acetate = 9 : 1) to give N-(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenylethyl)aniline 3a (188
mg, 75% yield) as a pale yellow oil.
N-(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenylethyl)-4-methoxyaniline 3b:pale yellow oil,
yield 72%. 1H NMR δ 3.71 (s, 3H), 4.10 (br. d, J= 6.6Hz, 1H), 4.82 (qd,
J= 7.6, 6.6Hz, 1H), 6.61 (m, 2H), 6.75 (m, 2H), 7.39 (m, 3H), 7.45 (m,
2H); 19F NMR δ -74.5 (d, J= 7.6Hz, 3F); 13C NMR δ 55.6, 61.7 (q, J=
29.8Hz), 114.8, 115.7, 125.1 (q, J= 282Hz), 127.9, 128.9, 129.1, 134.3,
139.5, 153.3; GCMS m/z 281 (M+), 280 (M+-H), 212 (M+-CF3), 211 (M+-CF3H),
121
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Tri- and Difluoromethylated Amines from Aldimines Using
(Trifluoromethyl)trimethylsilane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Prakash, G. K. Surya; Mogi, Ryo; Olah, George A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(16), 3589-3592

