$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To 2,2-dimethyl-4-pentenal (1.36 mL, 10.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2
were addedDMF (anhydrous, 10 mL), TMSCF3 (4.2 g, 30 mmol), and carbene
(34 mg, 0.10 mmol).The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 4 h.
HC1 solution (2 N, 12 mL) wasadded and the solution was stirred at room
temperature until all TMS protectedintermediate converted to product.
Water (60 mL) was added and the aqueous layer wasextracted with ether (40
mLx2). Organic layers were combined and washed withsaturated NaHC03
aqueous solution (30 mL), brine (30 mL), dried over MgS04. Solventswere
removed under vacuum to give the crude residue, which was purified by
silica flashchromatography (10% EtzO/pentane) to give yield 1.29 g, 71%.
1H NMR (CDC13, 400MHz) δ 5.80 (my lH), 5.11 (d, J = 11.36 Hz, lH), 5.10
(d, J = 17.2Hz, lH), 3.71 (q, J = 8.08 Hz, lH), 2.45 (brs, lH), 2.28 (dd,
J = 8.08, 13.64 Hz, lH), 2.05 (dd, J = 6.80, 13.60 Hz, lH), 1.04 (s, 6H).
13c (CDC13, 100 MHz) δ 134.1, 125.8 (q, JC-F = 282 Hz), 1 18.5,75.2 (q,
JC-F = 28 Hz), 44.2, 36.7, 23.2, 22.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
