$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for diastereoselective
addition to synthesize fluorinated sulfinilamines 2a-h.: Method A:. RFTMS
(RF = CF3, C2F5, 2.0 equiv) was slowly added to a mixture of the imine
(1.0 equiv) and tetrabutylammonium acetate (1.1 equiv) in THF (0.1 M) at
-20°C. Reaction mixture was then stirred at -20°C until TLC revealed the
disappearance of the starting material. Next, saturated NH4Cl solution
was added at low temperature, and the reaction mixture was warmed to room
temperature. The quenched reaction mixture was extracted three times with
ethyl acetate and the combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4. Solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the crude
mixture was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using mixtures
of n-hexane:ethyl acetate as eluents to afford compounds 2a-f. Compound
2a was synthesized following the method A described above starting from
1a (1 g, 3.0 mmol).
(R)-2-Methyl-N-[(S)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(6-iodobenzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)ethyl]propane-2-sulfinamide
(2e). Compound 2e was synthesized following the method A described above
starting from 1e (356 mg, 0.94 mmol). Compound 2e as a white solid, yield
300 mg, 71%. M.p. 198-200°C. [α]25D= -66.6 (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.22 (s, 9H), 3.60 (d, J=7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.32 (dq, J=7.0 Hz,
7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.00 (dd, J=1.2 Hz, 2.8 Hz, 2H), 6.89 (s, 1H), 7.29 (s, 1H).
19F NMR (282.4 MHz, CDCl3) δ -73.60 (d, JFH=6.8 Hz, 3F). 13C NMR (75.5
MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.2 (CH3), 57.0 (C), 65.0 (q, 2JCF=31.0 Hz, CH), 89.6 (C),
102.2 (CH2), 107.4 (CH), 119.2 (CH), 124.6 (q, 1JCF=282.2 Hz, CF3), 129.9
(C), 149.0 (C), 149.3 (C). HRMS (EI) calcd for C13H16NO3F3SI [M++H]:
449.9842, found 449.9853.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
