$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Using 3a: To a stirred solution of 1a (30.0
mg, 0.18 mmol), 3a (10.5 mg, 0.018 mmol) and TMAF (3.3 mg, 0.035 mmol) in
toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1, 0.5 mL) was added Me3SiCF3 (52.2 μL, 0.35 mmol) at -
80°C under N2 atmosphere. After reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at
the same temperature, it was quenche-d with sat. NH4Cl aq. Aqueous layer
was extracted with AcOEt (5 mL x 2), and the combined organic layers was
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced
pressure to furnish the crude 2a as a trimethylsilyl ether. The
trimethylsilyl ether was treated with TBAF (50.6 mg, 0.19 mmol) in THF
(1.5 mL) at room temperature for 1h. The resulting mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (acetone/n-hexane= 10/1) to give 2a (41.7
mg, 98%, 87% ee) as a white solid.
1.1.1-trifluoro-2-(naphthalen-2yl)propan-2-ol (2a) Using 3c: The reaction
of 1a (30 mg, 0.18 mmol) in toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1, 0.5 mL) with Me3SiCF3
(52.2 μL, 0.35 mmol) and TMAF (1.6 mg, 0.018 mmol) using 3c (10.5 mg,
0.018 mmol) was obtained antipode of 2a (29.7 mg, 70%, 77% ee). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.88 (s, 3H), 2.50 (s, 1H), 7.46.7.54 (m, 2H), 7.66 (d, J =
8.4Hz, 1H), 7.78.7.92 (m, 3H), 8.05 (s, 1H); 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ .80.7 (s,
3F); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 24.2, 75.0 (q, J = 29.1 Hz), 123.3 (d, J = 1.6
Hz), 125.4 (d, J = 1.2Hz), 125.46 (q, J = 284.5 Hz), 126.2, 126.8, 127.3,
127.9, 128.2, 132.6, 132.8, 135.5; IR (KBr) 3525, 3066, 3004, 1601, 1507,
1462, 1387, 1281, 1166, 1092, 957, 929, 899, 863, 824, 753, 719, 670
cm-1; MS (EI, m/z ) 240 (M+); The ee of the product was determined by
HPLC using a OD-H column (n-hexane/i-PrOH = 95/5, flow rate 0.5 mL/min, λ
= 254 nm, τmin = 18.1 min, τmaj = 27.2 min), 77% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 77% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
